            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0640" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12494: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-28T14:00:00-05:00">October 28, 1933—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>359. Your 819, October 28, 1 p.m., paragraph 3. In Department’s 358, October 27,
                    4 p.m., the phrase “officials of other governments” should be read to include
                    Chinese officials.</p>
                <p>You should endeavor in conversations with British officials to persuade them to
                    take the same position which you, acting under Department’s instruction as given
                    in 358, will take.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
